  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To spot hail damage on a roof, look for random pockmarks, missing shingle granules, and dents on soft metal accessories like gutters and vents.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "look for random pockmarks, missing shingle granules, and dents on soft metal accessories like gutters and vents"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Check Ground-Level Signs First"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Before climbing a ladder, look for external clues around your property that indicate large hail hit your home:",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Gutters and downspouts: Look for visible dents, dimples, or scratches on metal gutters and downpipes."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Granules in runoff: Check the bottom of your downspouts or inside the gutters for a build-up of sand-like shingle granules."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Other metal or glass surfaces: Inspect your air conditioner\u2019s outdoor condenser fins, metal mailboxes, window screens, garage doors, and patio furniture for random pockmarks.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Inspect Asphalt Shingles (Up Close)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you can safely access the roof, look closely at the asphalt shingles for these classic signs:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Dark spots or bruises: Impacts leave circular \"bruised\" areas where the protective mineral coating is knocked off."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Exposed fiberglass: Bald patches show the dark, shiny, or rough fiberglass/asphalt mat underneath."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Soft spots: Press gently on the shingle; hail-damaged spots often feel soft or spongy, similar to a bruised apple."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Random distribution: Hail strikes appear scattered and random rather than following a straight line or uniform wear pattern.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "3. Check Other Roofing Materials"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Metal roofs: Look for visible, repeated dents across the metal panels or standing seams."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tile or slate roofs: Look for sharp, circular cracks, chips, or broken corners."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Vents and flashing: Check roof vents, chimney caps, and valley metal for dings and bent edges.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              5,
              6
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "4. Look for Interior Leaks"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Check your attic and top-floor ceilings after a heavy storm for new water stains, damp insulation, or active leaks where the roof seal has failed.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Here is a short video showing what to look for on soft metal components and roof fixtures during an inspection:"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prepare for a roof inspection or insurance claim if you tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of roofing material you have (asphalt, metal, tile, etc.)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What size hail you think fell during the storm"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "If you are noticing any active leaks inside your home"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
